ze0: INTC/INT2 model at 0xff802000/0xff804000 and TMU ch0-2 (TODO M8.B1).

Adds hw/sh4/ze0_intc.c (TYPE_ZE0_INTC): the INTC block (ICR0, INTPRI,
ICR1, INTMSK0/1 with INTMSKCLR0) and the INT2 block (INT2PRI0..7,
INT2MSKR write-1-masks / INT2MSKCR write-1-unmasks) as read by the EU2011
nk.exe OAL (BSPIntrInit fn 0x8803dc70, timer hook fn 0x8803d168).  TMU
ch0-2 (hw/timer/sh_timer.c, 0xffd80000) are wired to INTEVT 0x400/0x420/
0x440 behind INT2 bit 1, level = INT2PRI0 field >> 1 (bits 20:16, 12:8,
4:0).  The model is the CPU's intc_handle.

hw/intc/sh_intc.c: struct intc_source gains `prio`; a source with prio != 0
is delivered only above SR.IMASK (highest first), prio == 0 keeps the old
first-pending rule, and an all-masked scan returns -1 instead of asserting.
r2d is unaffected (its sources are prio 0).

Evidence and controls: docs/experiments/EXP-2026-11-20-M8.B1-intc-model.md
(C-1310..C-1313).  Base: QEMU 8.2.10 + the earlier patches (sorts after
ze0-0002).

This file is the QEMU 11.1.3 form of the patch (TODO M8.A11): the text
above was written for the 8.2 series, where the patch was first made;
API names in it that 11.x renamed are listed in PORT-11.1.md.  Base: tag
v11.1.3 plus the earlier patches of this directory, in sorted order.

